From accfed5a18dd9ed4a37d4f2a009c51940ff22978 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:33:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/29] Challenger: shadow book in the server engine, its
 record section, the Blotter's separate track record, the on/off golden
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The challenger scores the rows the scan already built (no request of its own), through the same gates and
seat rules in a book of its own, settles with the ledger's path reads and rules, and is shown apart as
"Challenger · shadow". CHALLENGER_SHADOW=0 turns it off. The golden runs a recorded session through the
engine's late path with the shadow off and on: the live rows, scores, would-calls and seats are identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MshbhmXwtP12E5EwN7jDwQ
